<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Using Point-Slope Form to Write the Equation of a Line</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00305</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Using Point-Slope Form to Write the Equation of a Line</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e795ae3c-1223-42fc-aef7-4d4ab02cfe7c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Your teacher will assign you one pair of the points shown.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Points for Line A: <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo>,</m:mo>
            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo>,</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00015">Points for Line B: <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo>,</m:mo>
            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mn>1</m:mn>
            <m:mo>,</m:mo>
            <m:mo>–</m:mo>
            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00003">Use your assigned points to find the following:</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Find the slope of the line.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00006">Line A: slope: <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00016">Line B: slope: <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00007">Remember to use the slope formula to find the slope: <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msub>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msub>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:msub>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    </m:msub>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:msub>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msub>
                    <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                    <m:msub>
                      <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                    </m:msub>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
            .</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Write the equation of the line in slope-intercept form.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00010">Line A: equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00017">Line B: equation <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00011">Remember to use the point-slope form for the equation of the line to
            write the equation: <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:msub>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msub>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:msub>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msub>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>–</m:mo>
                <m:msub>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:msub>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>. Write
            the equation in slope-intercept form <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, where the slope is <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">Compare your equation to your partner’s equation. What were some
            things that were the same? What were some things that were different</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00014">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>Both lines have a negative slope.</item>
            <item>Both lines have the same slope.</item>
            <item>The <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercepts are
              different.</item>
            <item>The <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercepts have
              opposite signs.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>